# Edge functions

Client-callable mail entry is `notify`. It loads recipient and template data from the DB, then calls `send-transactional-email` with the service role.

```ts
// Browser / authenticated client — IDs only
await supabase.functions.invoke("notify", { body: { kind: "registration", registration_id } });
```

- `send-transactional-email` must stay service-role-only. Do not accept recipient/body from the client (phishing relay).
- Queue path: `enqueue_email` / `process-email-queue`. Reminders: `schedule-event-reminders` (24h and 1h flags on the event).
- AI: `generate-cover-image`, `generate-event-page`, `regenerate-landing-section`. Upload results to existing storage; persist URLs on rows.
- Public URLs inside functions use `PUBLIC_APP_URL`. Sender domain is configured in the email function — do not change it casually.
- Match existing Deno `serve` + CORS patterns. Rebuild `types.ts` if you add RPCs; this repo has no SQL migrations.
